# Git Commits — No Co-Author

When making git commits, do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any other co-author trailer to the commit message.

Use plain commit messages only. Example:

```
Vendor SingleApplication: remove submodule, add .gitignore, document in UpdateWallet
```

Not:

```
Vendor SingleApplication: remove submodule, add .gitignore, document in UpdateWallet

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```
